@startuml
' Phase 10 — Console: planned infrastructure. Authored at phase start.
' Copy to summary.uml at phase end and edit to the as-built state.

title Phase 10 — Console (planned)

skinparam componentStyle rectangle

package "aa-console (Go; imports contracts only)" as console {
  component "console (types + errors + clock + Surface)" as core
  component "client (control-plane HTTP/JSON + deterministic fake)" as client
  component "command (typed commands + idempotency + audit)" as command
  component "view (read models / browsing)" as view
  component "approval (explicit gate decisions)" as approval
  component "config (workflow + tool/plugin management)" as config
  component "tui (deterministic text surface)" as tui
  component "web (local stdlib HTTP surface)" as web
  component "app (surface wiring + entry point)" as app
}

package "aa-contracts (v1 schemas + openapi control plane + rpc spec)" as contracts
component "control-plane server (loopback HTTP/JSON; composition, deferred)" as server
package "aa-kernel (orchestrator, learning reports)" as kernel
package "aa-memory (issues, strategies, records)" as memory
package "aa-visualizer (sessions, replay)" as visualizer
package "aa-sync (compute/sync nodes)" as sync
package "aa-toolbox (tools, workflows)" as toolbox
component "desktop surface (Wails; deferred)" as desktop

contracts --> core
core --> client
core --> view
client --> command
core --> command
command --> approval
client --> approval
core --> config
command --> config
core --> tui
view --> tui
command --> tui
core --> web
view --> web
command --> web
tui --> app
web --> app
client --> app
client ..> server : HTTP/JSON (loopback, bearer)
kernel --> server
memory --> server
visualizer --> server
sync --> server
toolbox --> server
desktop ..> core : implements Surface (deferred)

note right of core
  ADR-P10-001: the console depends
  only on contracts and the external
  control-plane HTTP API. It imports
  no module internals and calls no
  inter-module RPC. D5/D22.
end note

note bottom of client
  ADR-P10-003: the control-plane
  client is a seam; a deterministic
  fake stands in for tests and offline
  use, and an httptest server exercises
  the OpenAPI paths. The real server
  is a composition concern (deferred).
end note

note bottom of command
  ADR-P10-005: every write carries an
  idempotency key derived from the
  command contract id and is audited.
  Approved commands are replayed
  safely.
end note

note bottom of view
  ADR-P10-004: views are pure,
  deterministic projections of client
  responses, ordered by id/sequence,
  never the wall clock, so renders are
  golden-testable.
end note

note bottom of approval
  ADR-P10-006: approvals and gates
  state their consequences and require
  an explicit decision; nothing is
  auto-resolved (D18).
end note

note bottom of config
  ADR-P10-008: workflows and tool
  manifests are data edited through the
  control plane, validated before write;
  no console code changes (D16/D17).
end note

note bottom of tui
  ADR-P10-007/009: the text surface
  renders the shared view layer with
  stable, golden-tested output.
end note

note bottom of web
  ADR-P10-007/009: the local web
  surface serves the same view models
  as semantic HTML with a plain-text
  alternative; accessibility first.
end note

note bottom of desktop
  ADR-P10-002/010: surfaces are
  pluggable behind one Surface
  interface; the Wails desktop surface
  is deferred and must be addable
  without changing other modules.
end note

@enduml
